  "construction_notes": [
    {
      "text": "Demolition of about 785,489 sq ft of existing retail; Target and the Century at Tanforan theater (75,800 sq ft, remodeled) are retained",
      "src": [
        "SRC-000403",
        "SRC-000400"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Master plan with a programmed area and two flex zones; optional 170-room hotel",
      "src": [
        "SRC-000400",
        "SRC-000403"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "City lists APNs 014-316-330, -310, -360, -080, -300 and 014-311-060.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001346"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Planning Commission agendas for October 20 and November 5, 2026 list the Tanforan item as recommendations to the City Council: certify the EIR, override the ALUC inconsistency determination, General Plan Amendment, PD zoning ordinance and Development Plan, Vesting Tentative Map, and a Development Agreement ordinance with Alexandria Real Estate Equities.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002137",
        "SRC-002136"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "November 5, 2026 staff report: the item was continued from October 26 after a California Public Utilities Commission letter dated October 21, 2026; staff concluded the CPUC comments do not require revising the Final EIR. The development agreement term is 15 years.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002136"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "San Bruno City Council regular meeting of November 10, 2026 was cancelled; notice gives the next regular meeting as December 8, 2026.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002138"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Planning Commission agendas list APN 014-316-060; the November 5, 2026 staff report lists 014-311-060. County parcel data has 014-311-060 (no situs address, owner ARE-San Francisco No 96 Holding LLC, Dayton Hudson Corp lessee) and no parcel 014-316-060.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002136",
        "SRC-002139"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "City press release, Nov. 19, 2026: master plan of up to 1,514 homes, up to 1.8 million square feet of office and research space, 100,000 to 150,000 square feet of retail, a potential 170-room hotel, and retention of Target and the cinema. If the ordinances are adopted Dec. 8, 2026, they take effect 30 days later; final mapping, demolition and individual building approvals follow.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-004283"
      ]
    }
  ],
